    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i spent my whole life thinking i was destined for something massive. coding, competitions, just constant grinding to be the best. but i just hit this wall. i realized i'm just... average. i'm just another dev. i'll never be a maverick or a legend. honestly, it feels like i've wasted every single second of my life just to end up being nothing special. being mediocre feels like a slow death.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Your feelings of inadequacy are valid, yet realize that \"average\" is often just a reflection of high expectations rather than a definition of your worth. Many successful professionals feel these same doubts, yet their impact on the world stems from consistency and authenticity rather than temporary fame. True mastery comes from finding purpose in your unique path, even if it doesn't lead to being a legend.",
